%[text] %[text:anchor:H_327926B0] ## Introduction
%[text] You local florist is having trouble with their flowers dying due to temperature and humidity conditions in their greenhouse. With your new knowledge of Arduino and MATLAB, you have been hired to help them implement a control system to monitor the temperature and humidity and help regulate it with a fan.
%[text] 
%[text] Before beginning this module, please ensure that you have downloaded the following support packages:
%[text] [Simulink Arduino DHT Sensor](https://www.mathworks.com/add-ons/62372d32-0e06-4c12-94b5-c1592ca9c6cb/?s_tid=srchtitle)
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_9EA3DB21] ## Constructing the Circuit
%[text] To help the florist, we will need three components other than our Arduino:
%[text] 1. An Arduino Board
%[text] 2. A DC motor with a fan    
%[text] 3. A DHT11 sensor (humidity and temperature sensor)      \
%[text] ![Exercise icon](text:image:1103) **Exercise.** Construct the circuit with the two components below:
%[text] 
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![DHT wiring diagram](text:image:34e6)
%[text]{"align":"center"} Wiring diagram for DHT sensor - this image was created using [fritzing-parts](https://github.com/fritzing/fritzing-parts/)
%%
%[text] ![Try this icon](text:image:2ba2) **Try.** Inform the board you are using and the pins used for the DHT sensor.
MyBoard  = "Arduino Uno"; %[control:dropdown:3758]{"position":[12,25]}
MyDHTPin = ""; %[control:editfield:92fd]{"position":[12,14]}
%%
%[text] ![Exercise icon](text:image:3a3a) **Exercise.** Wire the DC motor on a PWM pin.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Wiring DC Motor](text:image:41c1)
%[text]{"align":"center"} Wiring diagram for DC motor - this image was created using [fritzing-parts](https://github.com/fritzing/fritzing-parts/)
%%
%[text] ![Try this icon](text:image:9fed) **Try.** Inform the board you are using and the pins used for the DHT sensor
MyFanPin = ""; %[control:editfield:5435]{"position":[12,14]}
%[text]{"align":"center"} 
%[text] ![](text:image:0e76) **Reflect.** The digital pins on the Arduino will allow us to send PWM signals to the fan, and read temperature and humidity values from the DHT11 sensor.
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_79C165FD] ## Designing the fan control algorithmGreenhouseControl
%[text] You learned how to create, edit, and simulate models using block diagrams from the Simulink Onramp. Model-based design is powerful because it allows you to edit and simulate systems virtually before deploying them in real life. 
%[text] For the below exercises, you will employ Simulink to achieve your final result.
%[text] 
